  <entry>
    <content type="application/xml">
      <m:properties>
        <d:Id m:type="Edm.Guid">22222222-2222-2222-2222-222222222222</d:Id>
        <d:Title>Announcements</d:Title>
        <d:EntityTypeName>AnnouncementsList</d:EntityTypeName>
        <d:BaseTemplate m:type="Edm.Int32">104</d:BaseTemplate>
        <d:NoCrawl m:type="Edm.Boolean">false</d:NoCrawl>
        <d:Hidden m:type="Edm.Boolean">false</d:Hidden>
        <d:ItemCount m:type="Edm.Int32">2</d:ItemCount>
      </m:properties>
    </content>
  </entry>
  <!--
    Tripwire entry for two defects GetLists2013 used to have.

    - No <d:NoCrawl> element here at all, so GetLists2013 has to fall back to
      its default. That default was TRUE, where the modern GetLists defaults to
      FALSE, so this entry was wrongly excluded from crawling. The two entries
      above always supply NoCrawl explicitly, so nothing else exercises the
      default.
    - <d:Hidden> is true here. Hidden was read from the outer dataMap instead of
      the per-entry value map, so it always fell back to its own default of
      FALSE - silently wrong for this entry.

    Both are asserted by GetLists2013Test#test_parsesAllListsFromTheAtomFeed.
    Do not delete this entry: it is the only one that tells a correct default
    and a correct map from a coincidentally passing one.
  -->
  <entry>
    <content type="application/xml">
      <m:properties>
        <d:Id m:type="Edm.Guid">44444444-4444-4444-4444-444444444444</d:Id>
        <d:Title>Hidden No-NoCrawl List</d:Title>
        <d:EntityTypeName>HiddenNoNoCrawlList</d:EntityTypeName>
        <d:BaseTemplate m:type="Edm.Int32">100</d:BaseTemplate>
        <d:Hidden m:type="Edm.Boolean">true</d:Hidden>
        <d:ItemCount m:type="Edm.Int32">0</d:ItemCount>
      </m:properties>
    </content>
  </entry>
</feed>
